 {id:'s110', name:'Amazake Chaya (old Tokaido tea house)', area:'Hakone', lat:35.2020, lng:139.0487, cat:'Tea house', hours:'07:00–17:30, every day; 30-car lot', best:'Nov 19 14:00', use:'A thatched tea house on the old Tokaido highway, serving since the early 1600s: unsweetened rice-koji amazake and chikara-mochi grilled over charcoal. Your request; 25 min', day:4, you:true, dup:'p102'},
 {id:'s111', name:'Tenzan Tohji-kyo (Hakone Yumoto day onsen)', area:'Hakone', lat:35.2249, lng:139.0887, cat:'Day onsen', hours:'09:00–22:00', best:'Nov 19 14:45, optional', use:'Outdoor hot-spring baths by the Haya river used by locals, ¥1,450. Skip it and you are back in Tokyo an hour earlier', day:0},
 {id:'s112', name:'OnlyJDM Car Rental, Tokyo North store (足立区南花畑)', area:'Adachi', lat:35.79194, lng:139.82304, cat:'JDM rental', hours:'10:00–18:30', best:'BOOKED: Nov 18 10:00 → Nov 19 by 18:30', use:'2015 Mazda MX-5 ND 1.5 S Leather Package, 6-speed manual: ¥17,000 a day; cover Lite ¥3,000 (third-party only) or Premium ¥9,000 a day; 200 km per 24 h then ¥55 per km; ¥50,000 refundable deposit; 23+ with 3 years on a manual licence; physical licence + passport + IDP. 3-7-16 Minamihanahata, Adachi-ku, 10 min on foot from Rokucho on the Tsukuba Express. Licensed operator (J Project Co., Ltd.), Google 5.0 from 751 reviews, English support, info@only-jdm.com', day:3},
 {id:'s113', name:'Hakone Turnpike, Odawara gate (アネスト岩田ターンパイク箱根)', area:'Odawara', lat:35.2424, lng:139.1398, cat:'Toll road', hours:'05:30–22:30', best:'Nov 19 13:50, the climb', use:'The 13.8 km toll road from Hayakawa in Odawara up to Daikanzan at 1,011 m: long sweeping bends, Sagami Bay opening up behind you, Fuji ahead near the top; the road the Japanese car magazines test on. ¥900 each way for a normal car, pay at the gate', day:4},
 {id:'s114', name:'MANGA ART HOTEL, TOKYO (Kanda)', area:'Kanda', lat:35.6934, lng:139.7641, cat:'Capsule hotel', hours:'Check-in 16:00–23:00, check-out 05:00–11:00', best:'Nov 19, booked', use:'Booked on Booking.com for the night of Nov 19: bunks set among shelves of manga, Kanda Nishiki-cho 1-14-13. Your pick. 15 min walk from Akihabara, 5 min from Awajicho for the Marunouchi line to Tokyo station; check in before 23:00', day:4},
 {id:'s115', name:'Kyoto ryokan night (e.g. Ryokan Shimizu)', area:'Kyoto station', lat:34.9873, lng:135.7525, cat:'Ryokan', hours:'Check-in 15:00', best:'Nov 20 or 21, instead of a Len night', use:'Your note on Sawanoya said you want a good ryokan if Kyoto has one: Ryokan Shimizu (5 min from Kyoto station, tatami single with bath, about ¥12,000–16,000) or Nishiyama Ryokan (central, ¥15,000+) are the honest small ones. The 3-day weekend is filling: book this week or let it go', day:5},
 {id:'s116', name:'Shiraito Falls (白糸の滝)', area:'Fujinomiya', lat:35.3123, lng:138.5878, cat:'Waterfall', hours:'Car park 09:00–17:00, ¥500', best:'Nov 18 16:00', use:'A 150 m wide curtain of Fuji spring water sliding off a lava cliff into a blue-white pool: the blue water you asked for, 30 min south of Lake Motosu and on the way to Ito. 10 min walk down from the car park; free', day:3},
 {id:'s117', name:'Flash Disc Ranch', area:'Shimokitazawa', lat:35.6612, lng:139.6686, cat:'Used records', hours:'12:00–20:00, closed Wed', best:'Nov 17 14:45', use:'The cheap-vinyl shop: thousands of used LPs on the 2nd floor of a scruffy building south of the station, most ¥500–1,500, deep rock and prog bins. This is where a cheap Pink Floyd lives; Disk Union is pricier', day:2},
 {id:'s118', name:'Jimbocho curry: Bondy or Kyoeido', area:'Jimbocho', lat:35.6957, lng:139.7576, cat:'Curry', hours:'11:00–21:00', best:'Nov 24 12:30', use:'Your note calls Jimbocho the best curry in Japan: Bondy (European beef curry with a boiled potato, ¥1,500, queue from 11:30) or Kyoeido (Sumatra curry since 1924, ¥1,100). Both inside the book town', day:9},
 {id:'s119', name:'Nigatsu-do sunset balcony (Nara)', area:'Nara', lat:34.6893, lng:135.8449, cat:'Viewpoint', hours:'24 h, free', best:'Nov 21 16:45, sunset 16:50', use:'The wooden balcony above Todai-ji faces west over the whole Nara basin: the classic Nara sunset, lanterns, no ticket, deer on the stone path up. 10 min on foot from the Great Buddha hall', day:6},
 {id:'s120', name:'Yakiniku Ushigoro Ginza (wagyu alternative)', area:'Ginza', lat:35.6716, lng:139.7650, cat:'Yakiniku', hours:'17:00–23:00', best:'Nov 23 evening, instead of the Blue Room', use:'If "10/10 wagyu" means the beef and not the hotel room: Ushigoro grills A5 kuroge wagyu at the counter, omakase courses ¥11,000–16,000, solo diners fine. Book on their site; Ginza is on the way back from Omotesando', day:8},
 {id:'s121', name:'Kyoto Samurai Experience at Waraku', area:'Mibu, Kyoto', lat:35.0083, lng:135.7357, cat:'Sword experience', hours:'Sessions 10:00, 13:00, 15:00; book ahead', best:'BOOKED: Nov 20 10:00–11:45', use:'Booked on Nov 11. The listing you found: 1 h 45 in a historic samurai residence. Samurai dress, form practice with a training sword, cuts at a target, Zen sitting, antique swords up close; staff send photos the same day. You paid ₹10,634 on Airbnb; 4.97 from 655 Airbnb reviews. A training sword, not a live blade: police guidance since December 2024 ended real-blade cutting for visitors in Kyoto', day:5, you:true}
